@startuml architecture
' Who computes what of the new UI, from level 0 at the top to the view models at the bottom,
' see README.md in this package. Arrows point to what is read; dashed arrows to the facts offered.
' Decisions of the user are kept in stores in the DataStore, left out here.
' Each repository and view model computes its analyses in a Memo, again only for a new input.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam linetype ortho
top to bottom direction

database "Database\n(TransactionProvider)" as db

package "shell: NextData (once per process)" as nextData {
  [ProviderLedgerSource] as ledgerSourceImpl
  [ContractRepository] as contractsRepo
  [BalanceRepository] as balanceRepo
}

package "ledger" {
  interface LedgerSource
  artifact Ledger
  artifact Catalog
}

package "facts" as factsPackage {
  artifact ContractFacts
}

package "view models (…Feature of the shell)" as viewModels {
  [ContractsViewModel] as contractsVM
  [BalanceViewModel] as balanceVM
  [FixedTransactionsViewModel] as fixedVM
}

note as memo
  Each analysis: input (data class) →
  **Memo** → result, computed again
  only for a new input, see README
end note

note as composition
  **NextData** creates the repositories once per
  process, so widgets and notifications can read
  them; the **…Feature** entries of the shell create
  the view models with what they read (viewModelsOf).
end note

' Level 0: read once for all
db <-- ledgerSourceImpl : transactions with tags\nand split parts, accounts,\nIBANs, categories, tags
ledgerSourceImpl -down- LedgerSource : provides
LedgerSource --> Ledger
LedgerSource --> Catalog

' Level 1
contractsRepo -up-> LedgerSource
contractsRepo ..> ContractFacts

' Level 2
balanceRepo -up-> ContractFacts

' View models show their repository
contractsVM -up-> contractsRepo
balanceVM -up-> balanceRepo

' View models that offer nothing read what they show themselves
fixedVM -up-> db : paged transactions

@enduml
